{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1347588-having-trouble-with-some-npc-concepts","id":1347588,"title":"Having trouble with some npc concepts","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-11-10T18:43:44-08:00","id":1347588,"title":"Having trouble with some npc concepts","content":"I'm working on a collection of npcs for a chronicle I'll be starting up soon and i'm struggling to figure out what seemings and kiths some of them should be. There are a few that just don't seem to fit any of the seeming or kith descriptions. The chronicle is set during 1812 in southern germany, which is why the descriptions may be a little archaic.<br /> <br /> The first is a frumpy motherly type who's a gossipy people person. She's spring court and has a knack for getting people to open up to her. She's always available to be a shoulder to cry on, and likes to help people suffering from emotional pain. Think something like Mrs. Potts from beauty and the Beast. For her Durance she would have been something like a nursemaid/governess. I'm thinking Playmate for the Kith, but I have no idea what seeming she should be. Wizened kind of fits but she's not a crafter or builder. Fairest kinda, but she's not &quot;stately and elegant&quot;.<br /> <br /> A jester of the spring court who is always trying to lighten the mood with jokes and tricks. I was originally thinking a Beast (bear) Playmate, but Beasts are meant to be &quot;Savage survivalists, passionate and deadly&quot; which is not what i want at all. I know that not all Beasts are animals and not all animals have to be Beasts, but even if I keep the dancing bear thing, what seeming would work?<br /> <br /> Or how about a summer king who is big, bold, and brash. He's a guy who loves to go off to war, but still has a tactical and strategic mind. I was thinking maybe Elemental (stone) for the Seeming, but there doesn't seem to be a Kith for &quot;blustery army general&quot;. I know Kiths are optional so I could I could just leave him without one.<br /> <br /> There are others I'm struggling with, but i didn't want to create too huge of a wall of text. Am I being too narrow in my views of what fits into each Seeming? Are there just some concepts that don't work with the Seemings that are available? I know there are some major holes in the Kiths that are available (which Kith and Kin is supposed to fill when it comes out in 10 years time) so I'm not surprised they can't cover all concepts, but as far as I know the 6 Seemings are all there will ever be. So what happens when none of the Seemings seem to fit a concept?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13542,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13542-shadowdragon","user":"Shadowdragon","date":". 11-11-2019, 06:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13542-shadowdragon","name":"Shadowdragon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-11T05:58:59-08:00","id":1347663,"title":"","content":"I think you're right that you're being too narrow in your view, and maybe getting a little too bogged down in the brief, fluffy descriptions that the authors put into the book. There's nothing in the mechanics that says Fairest have to be &quot;stately and elegant,&quot; and the mechanical aspects of that Seeming would be a great fit for your Mrs. Potts character. Playmate would be a fair kith choice, as would Chatelaine--even if the fluff isn't quite on point, the mechanics would work quite well. Ditto your Beast character: Even though the Seeming description leans heavily on the whole &quot;Red in Tooth and Claw&quot; thing, Beasts are supposed to represent the vast diversity of nature and there's nothing saying they can't be gentle or comical. Heck, even the Kith summary for Playmates has a description of a Beast like that.<br /> <br /> To your Summer King, you're looking at a different problem (which I guess you could also say is happening with your other two characters) in that you seem to be looking to sum up everything about the character in his Kith and Seeming, which would be a mistake. What a character is good at is more about how you allocate your attribute, skills and specialties than about Seeming and Kith. A Fairest Playmate or a Darkling Gristlegrinder might be a great general if they allocate a lot of dots to mental stats and take a specialty in tactics. Merits and contracts could play into this as well, but again, those aren't inextricably tied to your Kith or Seeming.<br /> <br /> Personally, I'm not happy with the small number of kiths currently available in the system. As a fan of 1e, I got used to having dozens of flavorful options to choose from and having only twelve now is a big letdown. That said, there's a lot you can do with only the official kiths. For instance, they don't have a stone-themed kith for today's earthy Elemental, but if you strip away the fluff (maybe to the point of renaming it), the Snowskin kith works pretty well. Or you could look at the broad range of fanmade kiths, or heck, even make one of your own. But whichever way you go, remember that a character's Kith and Seeming are meant to help you expand your character ideas, not limit them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12108-gscrap","name":"gscrap","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12108_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-22T10:03:47-08:00","id":1350251,"title":"","content":"Like gscrap said, there is no need to get bogged down with the narrow number of kiths. The 12 listed are really only examples, and chapter 7 has to rules for making your own. Basically each kith just gets one skill gets exceptional successes at 3 instead of 5 when used a particular way, and some unique power that costs 1 point of glamour to use.<br /> <br /> Also remember your the storyteller. It's your world. Your npcs for the most part never need to be fully stated out, as long as you have a good idea of what they are and are not good at, and keep it consistent. Best to know their dice pools for what that will be doing, fully stat out any npcs you use alot or are part of the partys motley. <br /> <br /> For example your &quot;flumpy motherly&quot; character. (Also winter could fit her well as they make good shoulder to cry on, being experts on sorrow) You could make any seeming fit.<br /> Beast: She could have been a wet nurse at the nurser and have aspects of an animal that is protective of its young and has large litters. (Or a momma bird, protecting it's eggs, or a spider)<br /> Darkling: (Think Addams family) She taught her keepers children, but taught them wrong from right, how to steel, misbehave, lie and get up to mischief.<br /> Elemental: She's made of wood, wool, and blankets. Each legs have a large backwards curve to them so she can rock back and forth like a rocking chair to keep the children from crying.<br /> Fairest: She was a governess at finishing school for True Fae's offspring. She had to teach the unruley creatures etiquette, social grace, and manners. <br /> Ogre: You were the protector of the wormy children of the gentry lord and lady. They were many creatures trying to eat the tasty creatures, and she crushed every bug that came after them.<br /> Wizend: As a nurse maid she always had to make stories to keep the fae spawn interested, or constant craft new clothing as they grew. (Could have he always knitting when people go to talk to her)<br /> <br /> I find it helps to flush out the keepers a bit. If you know what they were like, what the looked like, what their realm was like, it can help you mold the design of your changelings. Also not all changeling need kiths. Feel free to just describe them how to feel they should look and try not to worry about the kiths for the npcs so much.<br /> <br /> Also, remember the keepers lack a fundamental understanding human concepts. A bear may be savage beast, but does the true fae the visited a human circus watching a bear balancing a ball on it's noise standing on a ball know that? Did it understand the bear and the ball are separate things? Do all bears have little jackets?<br /> <br /> It's also fun to play with duality and opposites when it comes to making fun npcs. Plus it's always nice to add a dash of horror and weirdness to the creatures of fae. (It is the wyrd after all) Giving your npc a weird habit or tick not and then. It will help flush the out for you and get into their heads. Perhaps a wizend will always tap a finger a foot anytime they hear a beat or repetitive sound to match it. <br /> <br /> Also Ogre could fit your summer king.<br /> folklore is also great inspiration for your changelings and keepers, as it's all biased off of fokelore, mythology, and dare I say, fairy tails after all. <br /> <br /> \u200bHope some of this helps.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6760,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6760-nlw162","user":"nlw162","date":". 11-22-2019, 01:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6760-nlw162","name":"nlw162","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-22T14:09:42-08:00","id":1350308,"title":"","content":"I think Wizened could definitely work for the first character. Or Fairest if you want to make her really pretty but also kind and empathetic. Not sure about the kith.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]}]}